<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Jan-May trade gap widens to CZK 64.619 BLN. [CORRECTED 08:15 GMT]</title>
<headline>Czech Jan-May trade gap widens to CZK 64.619 BLN. [CORRECTED 08:15 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects figures in middle table entitled &quot;By territory&quot;. The figures as initially reported referred to month of May 1997 rather than Jan-May period).</p>
<p>The Czech Republic posted a January-May trade deficit of 64.619 billion crowns, compared to a 55.257 billion crown deficit for the same period in 1996, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The CSU revised its January-April trade deficit to 53.421 billion crowns from a previously reported 53.652 billion.</p>
<p> CZECH FOREIGN TRADE   JAN-MAY 97    JAN-APRIL 97 JAN-MAY 96</p>
<p>  imports (CZK bln)     326.787    260.962 (261.652)  300.863</p>
<p>  exports		   262.168    207.541 (208.000)  245.606</p>
<p>  balance		   -64.619    -53.421 (-53.652)  -55.257</p>
<p>Note. All figures in billions of crowns on customs-cleared</p>
<p>basis and subject to revision. Previously reported</p>
<p>January-April figures in brackets.</p>
